{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he shall remove its crop with its feathers.</b> The מראה is the food inside the crop, and the priest would take the crop with its skin and the feathers on it and throw all of it to the place of the ashes. And the crop, which is the vessel of food, was not sufficient to wash it and burn it upon the altar, just as he would wash the entrails of an animal and burn them, because the bird goes here and there and feeds from robbery, unlike an animal; and so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: an animal that feeds from its owner's trough — concerning it is said ״והקרב והכרעים ירחץ במים והקטיר״; but a bird, which feeds from robbery — concerning it is said ״והסיר את מראתו״, that is to say, he shall cast away the innards that ate the robbery." "<b>And you should be roused</b> here by a great awakening for human beings concerning the matter of the substance of robbery. For just as the Holy One, blessed be He, distances from the altar the vessel of food in the bird and does not let it be brought near the altar of HaShem because it is a vessel of robbery, so too a person who has robbery in his hand — he shall not ascend and appear before Him and shall not merit to be in the company of the Holy One, blessed be He, unless he returns it. And the prophet revealed to us its severe punishment, which pursues him from this world and the world to come; as it is said (Jeremiah 17:11): ״עושה עושר ולא במשפט בחצי ימיו יעזבנו״ — that is, his wealth or the wealth shall leave him in half his days, and in his end, in the world to come, he shall fall from the Throne of Glory, which corresponds to the place of our Sanctuary, for the punishment of robbery prevents his soul from returning to its root, which is the Throne of Glory; and this verse is bound to its companion. And David, peace be upon him, already explained that those who merit to ascend before Him are those who are clean of robbery; as it is said (Psalms 24:3–4): ״מי יעלה בהר ה׳ ומי יקום במקום קדשו נקי כפים ובר לבב״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:00.876387006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}